# The command palette owns Enter; the ask card behind it does not.
#
# What Enter does when it DOES reach the card is submit: return_intent gives
# Submit the moment the answer is unblocked, submit_ask fires, and a
# successful resolve runs drop_attach_ask -- the card is retired and the
# question is gone for good. So the thing to assert the absence of is the
# card's disappearance, not that a note string is unchanged. The note read the
# same words before and after Enter no matter what happened, which is why
# deleting the `key ENTER` line used to leave this test green.
#
# `expect_no_text "Sending your answer..."` was worse than useless here:
# busyId is set and cleared inside one loader tick against the in-memory mock,
# so that string is never on screen twelve frames later whatever Enter did.
# It is gone.
#
# The control arm at the bottom presses the SAME key with the overlay closed
# and requires it to submit. Delete the Enter presses and that arm fails.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_ASK_DEMO=1 HANABI_TEST_OVERLAY=palette

require_thread t2
expect_text "The agent is asking"
expect_text "Answer any one of these to submit"
expect_text "Command palette"

focus_ui ask_option_q1_0
# Out of the focus ring while the palette owns the keyboard.
expect_not_focused ask_option_q1_0
key SPACE
wait_frames 12
expect_text "Answer any one of these to submit"

key ENTER
wait_frames 12
# No consequence. The card is still here and still unanswered: Enter did not
# reach it, so nothing was submitted and nothing was retired.
expect_text "The agent is asking"
expect_text "Answer any one of these to submit"

key ESCAPE
wait_frames 120
expect_no_text "Command palette"

# Control arm. With the palette gone the card has its keys back: SPACE picks...
focus_ui ask_option_q1_0
wait_frames 20
key SPACE
wait_frames 12
expect_no_text "Answer any one of these to submit"

# ...and ENTER, the very key the overlay refused, submits. A successful
# resolve retires the ask, so the card itself goes. If Enter never reaches the
# card -- unbound, uninjected, or simply not pressed -- the question is still
# on screen here and this fails.
key ENTER
wait_frames 40
expect_no_text "The agent is asking"
